In reference to the recent debate on whether artifacts make the game to
easy:
Why not have compile options that can keep gods from granting you weapons or
make artifacts less powerful.  Right now it seems that some people think the
Artifacts make the game too easy while others claim they have a hard time even
getting their hands on one.  Personally I've found that if the game seems to 
be getting to easy I move to a more challenging character.  Right now I'm
on my 7th Wizard and I have yet to make it past level 10!  An Artifact would
be nice, but even if I got one my HP are so abysmally low that I'ld probably
get whacked anyway.  And anyway, no one says you HAVE to use the artifacts or
ring of conflict or whatever.  The first time I ever played I had a barbarian
character and had no clue what a ring of conflict was for (infact I threw one
out thinking it was something bad!)  I sacrificed alot and was eventually 
given Cleaver but decided that my +6 long sword was better.  I used the wishes
on armor (GDSM and GoP) and cursed genocide scrolls.  The end game was a bitch
but I made it.  That was challenging, and it required no change to the game
itself, only the way I played.

